    {
      "id": "claim_82e5628882894fefa473d82c084bf2ba",
      "statement": "Host access to the provider is requested at runtime, not at install time: `requestOriginPermission` in `lib/settings.ts` converts a base URL into a Chrome match pattern (e.g. `https://api.openai.com/*`) and calls `browser.permissions.request`, so the granted scope is a single provider origin drawn from the `optional_host_permissions: ['<all_urls>']` pool.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://lib/settings.ts#L238-L257",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:439f6f017557d43500221a6ab7e74eb31d76e78b9bf6354920eeaedab95f0dfd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://wxt.config.ts#L21-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a48c522a35ff3a226b6d5f0de70e3fa517814af6ef6c14232d8f954f0c7998d2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_274117059cf74c6eb62aacc059be6d69",
      "statement": "The runtime host-permission request must stay inside a user gesture: `components/SettingsForm.tsx` calls `requestOriginPermission` synchronously in both `onSave` and `onLoadClick` (no `await` before the call), and the settings are still written when the user denies, with the form reporting `savedNoPermission` / `permissionDenied`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://components/SettingsForm.tsx#L145-L163",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f4d5886eaab6e0e4d5f4f5d12556ae44774c0b013a5063f67c75985aa9c70564:"
